        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete Section6 proof read, including the chain-selection Lemma6.3, generator reachability induction Theorem6.8 and the proper-submodule quotient in Theorem6.14. Generic means within each row below the top, distinct entries differ by no integer; top row is fixed and all lower entries change by integers. The selected basis comprises exactly tableaux whose Omega-plus set of nonnegative integral adjacent-row differences equals that of the starting tableau. Standard Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas and generic multiplicity-one construction are explicitly published background in Theorem5.2; component separation and unique generic simple module are supplied in Section5. The parameter-space equivalence-relation classification in the final sentence and later block counts are excluded."
      },
      "extra_source_paths": [
